<task id="052" project="ai-advanced-capabilities-analysis-hub-r1">
  <metadata>
    <title>Extend openSpaarkeAi (analysisId/worktype/regarding) + ribbon launcher</title>
    <phase>5 Entry model + record integration</phase>
    <gate>startable</gate>
    <status>completed</status>
    <rigor>FULL</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>New launch-param surface on the shared modal-open primitive + a new ribbon script on Matter/Project forms; drives record-driven entry (2b/2d); modifies .ts frontend surface consumed by the retirement phase (060/061).</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>sonnet</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>Mirror-first extension of a shipped precedent (`composeMode`/`openSpaarkeAiCompose` + `DocumentComposeLaunch`); the shape to copy is explicit — literal parameter addition, no novel design.</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>high</effort>
    <parallel-group>none</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>false</parallel-safe>
    <parallel-reason>Extends the shared `openSpaarkeAi` primitive that 050 (routing) and 053 (ADR-039 enforcement) depend on; sequence after 050/051 and before 053.</parallel-reason>
    <deps>050,051</deps>
    <tags>frontend, spaarkeai, ribbon, launch</tags>
    <estimated-effort>4-6 hours</estimated-effort>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>
    Add `analysisId`, `worktype`, and `regarding` params to `openSpaarkeAi` (spec §13.3 / FR-16), mirroring the shipped
    `composeMode`/`openSpaarkeAiCompose` precedent at `launch-resolver.ts:268`. Then add a `sprk_matter`/`sprk_project`
    ribbon script that reads the form record id and calls the extended `openSpaarkeAi` (mirror `DocumentComposeLaunch.ts:91`).
    Opening an existing analysis passes `analysisId`; opening new-in-record passes `worktype` + `regarding`=parent. The
    ribbon opens the three-pane modal (target=2) with regarding context. Sonnet 5: mirror the precedent literally; do not
    add params beyond these three.
  </prompt>

  <role>
    SPAARKE platform developer. Expert in the `launch-resolver` modal-open primitive, the `openSpaarkeAiCompose` mirror
    precedent, and Dataverse ribbon command scripts (`DocumentComposeLaunch`). Follow ADRs strictly.
  </role>

  <goal>
    `openSpaarkeAi` accepts `analysisId`/`worktype`/`regarding` (threaded through `buildLaunchUrl` into the `sprk_spaarkeai`
    web-resource `data`, mirroring `composeMode`); a `sprk_matter`/`sprk_project` ribbon command reads the form record id and
    calls `openSpaarkeAi` — opening the three-pane modal with regarding context (new-in-record: worktype + regarding=parent;
    existing: analysisId). Build is green; ui-tests below pass.
  </goal>

  <context>
    <background>
      §13.3 fixes the modal-open primitive as `openSpaarkeAi(params, target=2)` and instructs mirroring the
      `composeMode`/`openSpaarkeAiCompose` precedent to add `analysisId`/`worktype`/`regarding`. `launch-resolver.ts:268`
      (`openSpaarkeAiCompose`) shows the exact shape: force a mode/param, thread it via `buildLaunchUrl` into
      `navigateTo({pageType:'webresource', webresourceName:'sprk_spaarkeai', data}, {target:2, 80%×80%})`.
      `DocumentComposeLaunch.ts:91` (`openInCompose`) is the ribbon-script precedent: read the form record id from
      `primaryControl.data.entity.getId()`, normalize braces, call the launch primitive; never throw out of a ribbon callback.
      Task 050 established the four-case host mapping that consumes these params; task 051 added the subgrids that invoke this
      ribbon/open path.
    </background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file role="modify">src/solutions/SpaarkeAi/src/utils/launch-resolver.ts</file>
      <file role="new">src/solutions/SpaarkeAi/src/ribbon/ (new: AnalysisRecordLaunch.ts — sprk_matter/sprk_project ribbon script)</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/solutions/SpaarkeAi/src/utils/launch-resolver.ts:268 (openSpaarkeAiCompose mirror precedent)</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/solutions/SpaarkeAi/src/ribbon/DocumentComposeLaunch.ts:91 (openInCompose ribbon precedent)</file>
    </relevant-files>
    <dependencies>
      <dependency task="050" status="pending">Entry-matrix host routing — consumes analysisId/worktype/regarding to place 2b/2d in the correct host with pre-set context.</dependency>
      <dependency task="051" status="pending">Record subgrids on Matter/Project forms — the surfaces the ribbon launcher is invoked from.</dependency>
    </dependencies>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="project">SCOPE: extend `openSpaarkeAi` with exactly three params — `analysisId`, `worktype`, `regarding` — threaded through `buildLaunchUrl` mirroring `composeMode`; MUST NOT change the existing `openSpaarkeAi` signature semantics for current callers (additive only).</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-039">SCOPE: the ribbon launcher + param extension — record-driven opens go via `openSpaarkeAi` deep-link; MUST NOT route through `surfaceLaunchRegistry`.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">SCOPE: the ribbon script mirrors `DocumentComposeLaunch.openInCompose` — read `primaryControl.data.entity.getId()`, normalize braces, open empty/graceful on missing id; the callback MUST NOT throw (ribbon bars error out on throw).</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">SCOPE: new-in-record passes `worktype` + `regarding`=parent (2b); opening an existing analysis passes `analysisId` (2d). Do not cross the two payloads.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-021">SCOPE: the three-pane modal opened by the ribbon MUST render correctly in dark mode.</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <knowledge>
    <files>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-039-grounded-execution-closed-catalogs.md</file>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-021-fluent-design-system.md</file>
      <file>docs/architecture/ASSISTANT-SURFACE-LAUNCH-MECHANISM.md</file>
    </files>
    <patterns>
      <pattern name="openSpaarkeAiCompose mirror" location="src/solutions/SpaarkeAi/src/utils/launch-resolver.ts:268">
        Copy the pattern: default a param, spread into `buildLaunchUrl({...params, worktype, analysisId, regarding})`, open target=2 at 80%×80%. Additive to `openSpaarkeAi` — do not fork a whole new function unless the precedent did.
      </pattern>
      <pattern name="DocumentComposeLaunch ribbon script" location="src/solutions/SpaarkeAi/src/ribbon/DocumentComposeLaunch.ts:91">
        Read record id from `primaryControl.data.entity.getId()`, strip braces, guard unsaved/empty, call the launch primitive; never throw out of the callback.
      </pattern>
    </patterns>
  </knowledge>

  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="0" name="Context + rigor declaration">Declare FULL rigor; load ADR-039, ADR-021, and the surface-launch mechanism doc.</step>
    <step order="1">Study `openSpaarkeAiCompose` (launch-resolver.ts:268) + `buildLaunchUrl` and `DocumentComposeLaunch.openInCompose` (:91).</step>
    <step order="2">Add `analysisId`/`worktype`/`regarding` to the `openSpaarkeAi` params type and thread them through `buildLaunchUrl` into the `sprk_spaarkeai` `data`, mirroring `composeMode` (additive; existing callers unaffected).</step>
    <step order="3">Author the `sprk_matter`/`sprk_project` ribbon script (mirror `DocumentComposeLaunch`): read `primaryControl.data.entity.getId()`, normalize braces, guard unsaved, call `openSpaarkeAi` with worktype + regarding=parent (new) or analysisId (existing).</step>
    <step order="4">Verify the ribbon opens the three-pane modal (target=2) with regarding context; opening an existing analysis threads `analysisId`.</step>
    <step order="5">Run the ui-tests (incl. ADR-021 dark-mode); build `npm run build:prod` clean.</step>
    <step order="6">Update TASK-INDEX.md: set task 052 status to ✅.</step>
    <step order="7">Document any deviation in projects/ai-advanced-capabilities-analysis-hub-r1/notes/.</step>
  </steps>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>If threading `analysisId`/`worktype`/`regarding` additively breaks an existing `openSpaarkeAi` caller or requires diverging from the `composeMode` precedent (e.g. a new URL-param convention), STOP and escalate per CLAUDE.md §6 rather than reshaping the shared primitive silently.</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <justification>
    <existing>`openSpaarkeAiCompose` (launch-resolver.ts:268) + `DocumentComposeLaunch.openInCompose` (:91) — the shipped `composeMode` param-threading + ribbon-launch precedent.</existing>
    <extension>Yes — mirror the precedent: add `analysisId`/`worktype`/`regarding` to `openSpaarkeAi` and add one Matter/Project ribbon script; no new modal-open primitive or navigateTo abstraction is introduced.</extension>
    <cost-of-doing-nothing>No record-driven way to open or create an analysis in modal context (entry cases 2b/2d) — the ribbon on Matter/Project cannot pass regarding/worktype/analysisId to the SpaarkeAi modal, leaving record integration inert.</cost-of-doing-nothing>
  </justification>

  <ui-tests>
    <test name="ribbon new-in-record opens modal with regarding">
      <steps><step>On a saved Matter/Project record, click the Analysis ribbon button (new).</step></steps>
      <expected>The three-pane SpaarkeAi modal opens (target=2, 80%×80%) with `worktype` + `regarding`=the parent record threaded through the URL.</expected>
    </test>
    <test name="open existing passes analysisId">
      <steps><step>Open an existing analysis from the record subgrid.</step></steps>
      <expected>`openSpaarkeAi` is called with `analysisId`; the existing analysis loads in the modal.</expected>
    </test>
    <test name="unsaved-record guard">
      <steps><step>Invoke the ribbon on a new/unsaved form (no GUID).</step></steps>
      <expected>The callback logs a warning and does not throw; no broken command bar.</expected>
    </test>
    <test name="dark-mode (ADR-021)">
      <steps><step>Set the host theme to dark; open the modal via the ribbon.</step></steps>
      <expected>The three-pane modal renders correctly in dark mode.</expected>
    </test>
  </ui-tests>

  <tools>
    <tool name="npm">Build the SpaarkeAi code page (`npm run build:prod`).</tool>
  </tools>

  <outputs>
    <output type="code">src/solutions/SpaarkeAi/src/utils/launch-resolver.ts (analysisId/worktype/regarding params)</output>
    <output type="code">src/solutions/SpaarkeAi/src/ribbon/AnalysisRecordLaunch.ts (Matter/Project ribbon script)</output>
  </outputs>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">`openSpaarkeAi` accepts `analysisId`/`worktype`/`regarding` and threads them through `buildLaunchUrl` into the `sprk_spaarkeai` `data` (mirroring `composeMode`); existing callers are unaffected (additive).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given a saved Matter/Project record, when the Analysis ribbon button is clicked (new), then the three-pane modal opens with `worktype` + `regarding`=the parent record.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given an existing analysis opened from a record, when the launcher runs, then `openSpaarkeAi` is called with `analysisId`.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: on an unsaved form (no record id) the ribbon callback logs a warning and does NOT throw.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: the ribbon/open path uses `openSpaarkeAi`, not `surfaceLaunchRegistry` (grep-clean).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The modal renders correctly in dark mode (ADR-021); `npm run build:prod` is green.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>
    spec §13.3 / FR-16. Mirror `openSpaarkeAiCompose` (launch-resolver.ts:268) + `DocumentComposeLaunch` (:91). Consumed by
    the 050 host routing; enforced ADR-039-clean by task 053.

    COMPLETED 2026-07-29.

    **launch-resolver.ts**: added `analysisId`/`worktype`/`regarding` directly to the base `SpaarkeAiLaunchParams`
    interface (NOT a new extended interface like `SpaarkeAiComposeLaunchParams` — these params drive the SAME
    three-pane shell `openSpaarkeAi` already opens, unlike Compose which bypasses it). Threaded through
    `buildLaunchUrl` mirroring the `composeMode` block; braces stripped on `analysisId`/`regarding` like `entityId`.
    `openSpaarkeAi`'s signature is unchanged (still `SpaarkeAiLaunchParams`) — fully additive; back-compat tests for
    `openSpaarkeAi`/`openSpaarkeAiCompose` pass unmodified.

    **AnalysisRecordLaunch.ts** (new): two exported handlers mirroring `DocumentComposeLaunch.openInCompose`'s
    invocation-only shape (ADR-006) — `openNewAnalysisFromRecord(primaryControl, worktype)` (entry 2b: reads
    entityId/entityLogicalName from the form, guards unsaved/empty id, then guards empty `worktype` too — added
    during code-review Step 9.5 because a misconfigured ribbon StaticValue would otherwise silently degrade to the
    default cold-load instead of the hub, with no diagnostic; opens with worktype + regarding=parent) and
    `openExistingAnalysis(analysisId)` (entry 2d: opens with analysisId only). Neither function throws — mirrors
    `DocumentComposeLaunch`'s "ribbon callbacks must never throw" contract. The ribbon XML itself (CrmParameters,
    RibbonDiffXml) is explicitly task 071's job per its own POML — this task authors JS/TS only, confirmed against
    task 051's completion notes ("Task 052 ... is the task that will wire any custom open behavior").

    **Design resolution — worktype semantics**: confirmed via codebase research that a specific `worktype` value
    does NOT pre-select a hub card — `AnalysisHubWidget` always renders all cards; any non-empty `worktype` string
    only flips `main.tsx`'s `analysisMode` derivation to `"new"`. `openNewAnalysisFromRecord` therefore takes
    `worktype` as a caller-supplied parameter (from the ribbon's StaticValue CrmParameter) rather than hardcoding
    a value — the ribbon script stays invocation-only and has no opinion on which work type a button represents.

    **ADR-039 compliance**: no import or call of `surfaceLaunchRegistry` anywhere in the new/modified files; the
    docblock's explanatory mention of the name (to document why it is NOT used) mirrors the same convention already
    present in `WorkspacePane.tsx`/`ConversationPane.tsx`. Grep-verified clean.

    **Gates**: code-review — additive-only correctness confirmed (git diff stat: +78 lines, 0 deletions in
    launch-resolver.ts); found and fixed one real Warning (missing empty-`worktype` guard, described above) before
    completion. adr-check — ADR-006 (invocation-only, confirmed clean), ADR-039 (no registry routing, confirmed
    clean), ADR-021 (N/A — zero rendering/React code in these files, legitimate non-applicability not a scope-skip),
    ADR-028 (no manual token handling at the ribbon boundary, confirmed clean) — 0 violations.

    **Tests**: SpaarkeAi typecheck (`tsc-surface-gate`) — 0 surface-owned errors. Full SpaarkeAi jest suite — 81
    suites / 722 tests green (includes 8 new tests in `launch-resolver.test.ts` + 9 new tests in the new
    `AnalysisRecordLaunch.test.ts`, covering the POML's 3 ui-tests testable at this layer: new-in-record
    worktype+regarding threading, open-existing analysisId threading, unsaved-record guard). ADR-021 dark-mode
    ui-test is deferred to task 071's deployed-environment verification (no rendering surface exists in this
    task's files to test against).

    No deviation from the POML's directional steps or escalation trigger (the additive threading did not break
    any existing `openSpaarkeAi` caller; no divergence from the `composeMode` precedent was required).
  </notes>

  <execution>
    <skill>.claude/skills/task-execute/SKILL.md</skill>
    <protocol>Load knowledge files. Follow task-execute incl. Step 9.5 gates (FULL: code-review + adr-check).</protocol>
  </execution>
</task>
